%N A006372 Numbers of terms in expressions for coefficients of "Lovelock Lagrangians" (or "Gauss-Bonnet forms") in terms of Riemann-Christoffel curvature tensor and two of its contractions (viz., the Ricci curvature tensor and the Riemann curvature scalar) for n-dimensional differentiable manifolds having a general linear connection.
%C A006372 Also the number of unlabeled directed multigraphs on n vertices with indegree and outdegree 2 at every vertex, allowing loops and multiple arcs, including disconnected graphs. See Mathar.
%C A006372 Equivalently, the number of n X n matrices with nonnegative integer entries and all row and column sums equal to 2, up to simultaneous permutation of rows and columns. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 27 2026
%H A006372 C. Bogdanos, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.79.107501">Diagrammatic derivation of Lovelock densities</a>, Phys Rev. D 79 (10) (2009) 107501.
%H A006372 C. C. Briggs, <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9607033">A General Expression for the Quintic Lovelock Tensor</a>, arXiv:gr-qc/9607033, 1996-1997.
%H A006372 C. C. Briggs, <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9703074">A General Expression for the Quartic Lovelock Tensor</a>, arXiv:gr-qc/9703074, 1997.
%H A006372 R. J. Mathar, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.12477">2-regular digraphs of the Lovelock Lagrangian</a>, arXiv:1903.12477 [math.GM], 2019.
%F A006372 a(n) = Sum_{lambda |- n} F(lambda)/z(lambda), where lambda = (lambda_1, ..., lambda_r), g(i,j) = gcd(lambda_i, lambda_j), z(lambda) = Product_{k>=1} k^m_k*m_k!, and m_k is the multiplicity of k in lambda.
%F A006372 F(lambda) = [x_1^2*...*x_r^2*y_1^2*...*y_r^2] Product_{i,j=1..r} (1 - x_i^(lambda_j/g(i,j))*y_j^(lambda_i/g(i,j)))^(-g(i,j)). - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 27 2026
%e A006372 For n = 4, the partitions (1,1,1,1), (2,1,1), (2,2), (3,1), (4) give F(lambda) = 282, 18, 34, 6, 10 and z(lambda) = 24, 4, 8, 3, 4, respectively. Thus a(4) = 282/24 + 18/4 + 34/8 + 6/3 + 10/4 = 25.
%Y A006372 Cf. A006373, A045900 (conjectural), A306892 (2-regular digraphs).
